-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.00012110930401831865,-0.0005884823040105402,-0.00056429672986269,-9.321732068201527e-05,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-9.536738616588991e-07,0.0,-1.1801649634435307e-05,-0.0010926711838692427,-0.4696747064590454,-0.021643513813614845,-1.316985845565796,-0.1792626827955246,-2.0503786799963564e-05,-4.6491513785440475e-06,-7.068861305015162e-05,-5.960462772236497e-07,-5.960462772236497e-07,0.0,-2.3841855067985307e-07,0.0,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-0.0009289240115322173,-4.172316494077677e-06,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.9907753085135482e-05,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-3.576278118089249e-07,0.0,-3.576278118089249e-07,-7.974783511599526e-05,-6.687417771900073e-05,0.0,-0.0001546025014249608,-6.079655122448457e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,50,3948,400,17,89,488,600,284,22137,488,220,18,2418,220,17399,697,4226,304,279,1352,400,87,488,61697,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSolve $2z + i = iz + 3.$  Express your answer in the form $x + yi.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"692cd3dee02718a676bf1d21b0be708e857037f660bd49ecc07e73ff552154f5"},"seconds":31.46963882446289,"seed":1070701789923896720,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the equation $2z + i = iz + 3$, we first express $z$ in terms of $x$ and $y$, where $z = x + yi$ and $x, y$ are real numbers. We then solve for $x$ and $y$.\n\nStep 1: Substitute $z = x + yi$ into the equation.\n\\[\n2(x + yi) + i = i(x + yi) + 3\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Distribute the constants.\n\\[\n2x + 2yi + i = ix - y + 3\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Rearrange the equation to group real and imaginary parts on each side.\n\\[\n2x + i(2y + 1) = -y + 3 + ix\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Equate the real parts and the imaginary parts on both sides of the equation.\n\\[\n\\text{Real part: } 2x = -y + 3\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Imaginary part: } 2y + 1 = x\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Solve the system of equations. Start with the imaginary part equation to express $x$ in terms of $y$.\n\\[\nx = 2y + 1\n\\]\n\nStep 6: Substitute $x = 2y + 1$ into the real part equation.\n\\[\n2(2y + 1) = -y + 3\n\\]\n\\[\n4y + 2 = -y + 3\n\\]\n\nStep 7: Solve for $y$.\n\\[\n4y + y = 3 - 2\n\\]\n\\[\n5y = 1\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\frac{1}{5}\n\\]\n\nStep 8: Substitute $y = \\frac{1}{5}$ back into $x = 2y + 1$ to find $x$.\n\\[\nx = 2\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right) + 1 = \\frac{2}{5} + 1 = \\frac{2}{5} + \\frac{5}{5} = \\frac{7}{5}\n\\]\n\nThus, $z = \\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i$.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
